              "type": "text",
              "text": "In a sale, all prices in a shop are reduced by 10%. Later, the shop is offering an extra 25% off sale prices. Work out the price of a pair of shoes that cost $90 before the sale.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$60.75$",
      "worked": "The discount multipliers are $0.9$ and $0.75$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Sale price} &= \\$90\\times0.9\\times0.75\\\\\\text{Sale price} &= \\$90\\times0.675\\\\\\text{Sale price} &= \\$60.75\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
